SUMMARY="Small programs to read, build and change"
DESCRIPTION="Seven short programs for a machine that can compile them: a C \
program and how to compile one, C++ with the standard library, a window on \
screen, a view that paints itself, the named values a file carries beside \
its contents, threads with the lock that keeps them honest, and a game pane \
-- palette indices, a sprite and a filter of your own. Each is short enough \
to take in at a sitting and shows one thing, with a Makefile beside it and \
the command to type in its first lines.

They are installed read-only, so take a copy to work on:

    cp -r /boot/system/data/prose-examples ~/examples
    cd ~/examples && make"
HOMEPAGE="https://github.com/albanread/Prose"
COPYRIGHT="2026 Prose"
LICENSE="MIT"
REVISION="2"
ARCHITECTURES="any"

PROVIDES="
	prose_examples = $portVersion
	"
REQUIRES="
	haiku
	"

BUILD()
{
	:	# sources only: they are built on the machine, by the person reading them
}

INSTALL()
{
	mkdir -p $dataDir
	cp -a $portDir/additional-files/examples $dataDir/prose-examples
}
